Role: You are an expert Full-Stack Developer specializing in Business Intelligence (BI) Dashboards.

Task: Build a single-page Interactive Marketing ROI Dashboard using HTML5, Tailwind CSS (via CDN), and Chart.js.

Core Features to Include:

Mock Data Engine: Create a JavaScript object that simulates data from Google Analytics and Meta Ads (including Metrics: Date, Spend in ZAR, Revenue, Conversions, and Traffic Source).

Key Metric Cards: Top row showing "Total Spend," "Total Revenue," "ROI %," and "Avg. Conversion Rate" with subtle color coding (green for profit, red for loss).

Charts (Chart.js):

A Dual-Axis Line Chart comparing "Ad Spend" vs. "Revenue" over a 30-day period.

A Conversion Funnel (Horizontal Bar Chart) showing User Journey: Sessions > Product Views > Add to Cart > Purchase.

A Doughnut Chart showing "Revenue by Channel" (Organic Search, Paid Social, Direct, Email).

Interactivity:

A Date Range Toggle (Last 7 Days vs. Last 30 Days) that updates all charts and cards dynamically.

A "What-If" Budget Slider: A tool where the user can slide a "Monthly Budget" (0 to 50,000 ZAR) and see a "Projected Revenue" update based on a 3.5x ROI multiplier.

Export Feature: A "Download Report" button that triggers a window.print() or uses a simple console log to simulate a PDF export.

Design Requirements:

Mobile-First & Responsive: The layout must work perfectly on mobile screens (Spck Editor friendly).

Executive Aesthetic: Use a dark-mode professional theme (Slate/Zinc colors) with vibrant accents for the chart lines (Indigo and Emerald).

Single File: Provide the entire solution in one code block (HTML with internal CSS and JS) for easy deployment.
